Friday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy MSFT calls* Stocks rebound from steep losses as jobless =
data impressesStocks recovered from an early sell-down in choppy midday tra=
ding on Friday after a strong jobs report last month pointed to further rec=
overy prospects.The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 249.99 points, or 0.8=
1%, to 31,174.13. The S&amp;P 500 added 29.12 points, or 0.77% to 3,797.59,=
 and the Nasdaq Composite also gained 26.99 points, or 0.21%, to 12,750.46.=
 All three indexes made a complete reversal from heavy losses in morning tr=
ading.The showing followed sharp falls in the previous day after Federal Re=
serve Chairman Jerome Powell pledged to maintain ultra-loose monetary polic=
y amid a market shift in inflation expectations.At current levels, the Dow =
is heading for its first rise in two weeks while the S&amp;P and the Nasdaq=
 are bracing for third straight weekly losses. All three indexes hit record=
 levels last month.On Friday, data showed a 379,000 jump in nonfarm payroll=
s for February, following January's revised increase of 166,000, pointing t=
o an improving labor market. The unemployment rate fell slightly from 6.3% =
to 6.2%."Underemployment is still likely to put downward pressure on wages =
and thus also on inflation, at least this year and next," said Commerzbank =
economist Christoph Balz. "We do not expect the Fed to start making its mon=
etary policy somewhat less expansionary by scaling back its bond purchases =
until mid-2022."Still, the bond market remained volatile, with the US 10-ye=
ar Treasury yield spiking a few basis points early before retreating and si=
tting around 1.559% midday, down from 1.564% on Thursday. It climbed above =
one-year high of 1.6% last week.Meanwhile, Costco (COST) fell 2.5% after it=
s Q2 earnings missed market expectations that led to a slew of price target=
 cuts, including from UBS and JPMorgan. In addition to COVID-19 expenses, t=
he retailer also moved to raise its minimum wage to $16 this montPortfolio:=
 We came into today flat and now have one new idea for you.*NEW RECOMMENDAT=
IONMicrosoft Corp.(MSFT) March 230 calls-- Symbol: MSFT210319C00230000-- Or=
der: Buy at $5.90 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $8.10 lm=
t gtc and half at $10.90 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $4.10 stp, good a=
fter 10:30 a.m. ET only&nbsp;*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommen=
dations are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specifi=
ed month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Easter=
n only unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for the day only unl=
ess otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of the current s=
ession. Past results are no guarantee of future returns. All accounts may n=
ot achieve comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and speculativ=
e, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. A=
ll results are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading involves the =
risk of substantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wall Street Jo=
urnal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

